      "ts": "20260818_1920",
      "sender_norm": "POLITICO",
      "subject": "Brussels wants ‘Buy European’ but voters lean domestic",
      "subject_en": "Brussels wants ‘Buy European’ but voters lean domestic",
      "html": "data/pdfs/20260818_1920_Brussels_wants_‘Buy_European’_but_voters_lean_dome.html",
      "pdf": "data/pdfs/20260818_1920_Brussels_wants_‘Buy_European’_but_voters_lean_dome.html",
      "summary_en": "A new Public First poll shows voters in 23 of 25 EU countries favor domestic procurement preferences over a broader 'Buy European' standard, complicating Brussels' push for the Industrial Accelerator Act. While EU-wide support for a European preference sits just under 50%, national sentiment often outweighs it, except in Germany where both options draw weak support. The findings highlight political hurdles as the Commission seeks adoption of the bill, which covers 17% of EU economic output, by year-end.",
      "summary_ja": "Public First社の新たな世論調査によると、EU加盟25カ国中23カ国で有権者は「バイ・ヨーロピアン」よりも自国優先の公共調達を支持しており、欧州委員会が推進する産業加速化法に影響を与えかねない状況だ。EU全体では欧州製品優遇への支持が50%弱にとどまる一方、ドイツを除く多くの国で自国優先の意識が根強い。EU経済の17%を占める公共調達を巡るこの法案は年内の採択を目指しているが、世論の壁が課題として浮き彫りになっている。",
